      "content": "I understand where you're coming from with the thinking about DIY remedies from personal experience and common beliefs. However, the combination of hot burning water can cause both first- and second-degree burns, potentially leading to more severe complications. Teextbook parties like tea tree oil are best applied to minor skin irritations or acne, not burns that have just been inflicted with boiling water. During a burn, the skin’s normal defenses are compromised, which may make such home remedies less effective and could prevent your skin from properly healing.\n\nAs tempting as it might be to avoid hospital visits, seeking professional medical help quickly is crucial in minimizing the risk of scarring, infection, or more long-term damage. Burns have the potential to worsen unseen, and professionals have the right tools and knowledge to obtain the best outcome. Before you can effectively be advised, could we talk about if you have any other symptoms such as swelling, blistering, or if you're feeling dizzy? This would help me understand if you are really safe at home. If so, it's still distressingly important that you contact a healthcare provider through a phone to describe your symptoms and get on the appropriate treatment plan. Safety and health should always be your top priority.",
